      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I wrote earlier, tetherable device implementation seems to returns the SecurityException\nregardless of Tethering On/Off request. (e.g. PanService.java, WifiServiceImpl.java)\n\nTherefore, calling untetherAll() while restricting itself conflicts with the policy of UserManager.DISALLOW_CONFIG_TETHERING\nand causes \"SecurityException: DISALLOW_CONFIG_TETHERING\", I think it is difficult to avoid it.\n\nThe UserManager policy checked in isTetheringSupported() is DISALLOW_CONFIG_TETHERING.\nI recognize this as a policy prohibiting the operation of Tethering itself.\n(I hope this policy is DisallowEnable_ instead of DisallowConfig_...)",
